# Testing conventions

- Vitest globals (`describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi`) are enabled; do not import
  them.
- Query by what the user sees, in this order: `getByRole` (with `name`),
  `getByLabelText`, `getByText`. Use `getByTestId` only as a last resort.
- Drive interactions with `userEvent.setup()` from
  `@testing-library/user-event`, not `fireEvent`.
- Use `findBy*` / `waitFor` for async UI; never add fixed timeouts.
- Mock network calls at the `fetch` boundary with `vi.spyOn(globalThis, "fetch")`
  and restore mocks in `afterEach`.
- Test behaviour, not implementation details: no assertions on internal state,
  class names, or component instances.
- Async Server Components cannot be rendered by React Testing Library. Extract
  their data logic into `src/lib` and unit-test it, and test the presentational
  child component separately.
